DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The uuiiddiinnffoo family of functions is used to manage _u_i_d_i_n_f_o structures.
     Each _u_i_d_i_n_f_o structure maintains per uid resource consumption counts, in‐
     cluding the process count and socket buffer space usage.

     The uuiihhaasshhiinniitt() function initializes the _u_i_d_i_n_f_o hash table and its mu‐
     tex.  This function should only be called during system initialization.

     The uuiiffiinndd() function looks up and returns the _u_i_d_i_n_f_o structure for _u_i_d.
     If no _u_i_d_i_n_f_o structure exists for _u_i_d, a new structure will be allocated
     and initialized.  The uuiiddiinnffoo hash mutex is acquired and released.

     The uuiihhoolldd() function increases the reference count on _u_i_p.  _u_i_p's lock
     is acquired and released.

     The uuiiffrreeee() function decreases the reference count on _u_i_p, and if the
     count reaches 0 _u_i_p is freed.  _u_i_p's lock is acquired and release and the
     uidinfo hash mutex may be acquired and released.

